"about": [
  "Test vectors for the id of a new row (SPEC.md section 7, \"The id of a new row\"). One file, read by the linter's test (test/idvectors.test.js, which also holds a short reference maker that makes every case) and copied by any other writer that makes ids, to run the same cases against its own maker.",
  "The file is an object: `now` (a UTC time, the moment the reader pressed Add) and `uuid` (what `{uuid}` makes) for every case unless the case sets its own; `cases`, a list.",
  "A case: `name`; `format` (the block's idFormat); `ids` (every id the block holds at every depth, and the ids of adds still waiting; a string or a number each); `parent` (the parent row's id, or null for a top row); `fields` (the text in each box of the form, by field name; a field with no box or an empty box is missing or \"\"); and `expect`.",
  "`expect` is `{\"id\": X}` (a string, or a JSON number for the bare format {n}) or `{\"refuse\": WORD}`. The words: `invalid-format` (the format is not valid), `empty-slug` (a field part has no slug; `field` names the field), `clash` (the id made exists and no later second helps), `empty-id` (the id made is the empty string).",
  "An order of tests that never changes the answer: the format is checked first, then the parts are made left to right, then an empty id is refused, then a clash is looked for."
 ],
